SUMMARY:SILA
DESCRIPTION:In Greenland (Kalaallit Nunaat)\, the word Sila holds everything at once: the weather\, the breath\, the consciousness connecting all living things. This tender\, nonlinear documentary follows Inuit women moving through three hundred years of Danish colonialism\, including a medical program that inserted contraceptive devices into girls as young as thirteen without their consent. Their bodies became a site of colonial administration. Another film Premiere from Zaya&Maurizio Benazzo of SAND (science and nonduality)
URL:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/event/sila/
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High Street\, Sebastopol\, CA
CATEGORIES:Film
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://sebastopolcalendar.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Screenshot-2026-07-15-at-3.20.05-PM.png
